msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:59
msgid "Header your proxy sets"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:74
msgid "Only this header is read. A proxy overwrites the header it sets but passes any other header a visitor sends straight through, so choose the one your proxy documentation names: X-Forwarded-For for most load balancers and CDNs, X-Real-IP for a single nginx proxy, CF-Connecting-IP for Cloudflare, True-Client-IP for Akamai and some CDNs."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:77
msgid "Trusted proxy IPs / ranges (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:80
msgid "One IP or CIDR range per line - your proxy / CDN addresses. When set, the header is read only from requests that arrive from one of these addresses or from an internal address (loopback, private network or carrier-grade NAT, such as a load balancer or a local web server). With X-Forwarded-For, the client IP is the first address, reading from the right, that is neither. Leave empty if a single proxy sits in front (the rightmost forwarded address is used)."
msgstr ""

